    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1315">

                <pb facs="1129" n="1025" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.13/34.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to Costa Rica to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">San José</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 19, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have just learned that the Government of Salvador has invited the Governments
                    of Costa Rica, Guatemala and Honduras to send representatives to a meeting at
                    Salvador to consider and perhaps protest against the prospective acquisition by
                    the United States of the Fonseca and Dulce stations. The President of Costa Rica
                    replied that he would not send a representative unless the Government of
                    Nicaragua should be invited also. To this the Government of Salvador has not yet
                    responded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hale</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
